15. State types — important implementation rule

Treat these four states differently.

GAMEPLAY

* Player retains movement.
* Normal interaction remains enabled.
* Quest completion is based on player actions.

CINEMATIC

* Player control is locked.
* Normal interaction is disabled.
* Quest progression waits until the cinematic/animation has fully completed.
* Do not allow the player to interrupt or accidentally skip progression.

DIALOGUE

* Player movement is paused while talking to Mitchy.
* Quest state advances only through the intended dialogue action.
* Dialogue completion and quest progression should not trigger simultaneously unless explicitly defined.

USERTEST_TRANSITION

* Gameplay is fully paused.
* Used only for switching experimental conditions.
* No world-state progression should occur while this screen is active.

Do not implement a cinematic as a normal gameplay quest step that can be interrupted.

