SEQ — Single Ease Question: one item asked immediately after a task, usually “Overall, how difficult or easy was the task?” Good for immediate task-level usability, but too narrow for your five-question set.
ASQ — After-Scenario Questionnaire: typically 3 items after completing a task/scenario, focused on ease, time, and support/information. Much closer to your use case because it is designed for immediate post-task reaction.
PSSUQ — Post-Study System Usability Questionnaire: broader and longer, usually used after the whole session, so less suitable for your in-game micro-ratings.
CSUQ — Computer System Usability Questionnaire: also broader/system-level rather than immediate condition-level.
Single-item satisfaction / confidence ratings: common in usability testing, though not always part of one named validated scale.


